        "Abstract": "Open Japanese large language models have been trained on Japanese portions of corpora such as CC-100, mC4, and OSCAR. However, these corpora were not created for the quality of Japanese texts. This study builds a large Japanese web corpus by extracting and refining text from the Common Crawl archive. The corpus consists of approximately 312.1 billion characters, surpassing existing corpora for Japanese LLMs. Continual pre-training on Llama 2 and other base LLMs showed consistent improvements on Japanese benchmark datasets."
